course: dictionary
lesson: 9616
title: Strongly: force, feeling and smell
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Strongly is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens or how much. Its basic meaning is with a lot of strength or force. The words around it give you clues: «strongly built» tells you the thing is solid and sturdy.
explain: Strongly also describes feelings and opinions. «I strongly believe» means you are very firm about what you think, and «strongly agree» means you agree very much. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Strongly can also describe taste or smell. «The moonrat smells strongly of garlic or onion» means the smell is very noticeable. The same word works in all three ways, so look at the words next to it to find out which meaning is right.
fact: Strongly is an adverb: it tells you how something happens.
fact: «Strongly» means with a lot of strength or force.
fact: «Strongly» means very much or very firmly, as in «strongly agree».
fact: «Strongly» can mean with a strong taste or smell, as in «smells strongly of fish».
fact: The forms are strongly, more strongly and most strongly.
exercise: «The brain remembers frightening things strongly because noticing danger helped people survive.» What does strongly mean here? | Only for a short time | Very quietly and gently | With a loud noise | *Very clearly and firmly, so the memory stays
exercise: In a class survey you can choose «strongly agree». What does this answer show? | A dislike of surveys | *A very firm agreement | A small, unsure guess | A question about the survey
exercise: «The moonrat smells strongly of garlic or onion.» What does strongly describe? | The moonrat's name | The hedgehog | *The smell | The number of days
test: «Sunscreen should be at least SPF 30, which is the number that shows how strongly it protects.» What does strongly mean here? | *With great strength, so well it protects you | Only once a day | With a sweet smell | Very quietly and gently
test: A survey asks how you feel about reading. Which answer shows you firmly agree? | Mildly agree | Skip the question | *Strongly agree | Not sure
exam: In «a magnet attracts strongly when close», what does strongly mean? | With a sweet taste | *With great force, pulling hard | Only once | Very softly
